{
  "schemaVersion": 1,
  "purpose": "Complete mechanical baselines for incidental NPCs. Instantiation copies a template, rolls/chooses identity traits within bounded ranges, assigns a unique id, and immediately creates a valid memory/knowledge/relationship ledger.",
  "instantiationRules": [
    "Every on-screen NPC must exist as a sheet before they make a consequential roll or decision.",
    "Select the closest archetype; never create a statless narrative-only NPC.",
    "Vary level by at most +/-1 from template unless fiction clearly requires otherwise.",
    "Vary each attribute by at most +/-2 and each relevant trained skill by at most +/-1.",
    "Assign one immediate goal, one fear, one personality emphasis, a schedule/current plan, and knowledge limited to role/location.",
    "Create relationship entry to Rook on first direct interaction.",
    "Create memory entries for consequential interactions immediately.",
    "If named, recurring, quest-relevant, emotionally consequential, or seen again after a major interaction, promote to a dedicated NPC file and dedicated portrait."
